# Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded sine of BF16
#
# For |x| < 4096, x = x1 + x2, where x1 keeps the exponent and the upper 4 bits of the mantissa and x2 the exponent
# and the lower 3 bits. Then sin(x) = sin(x1) cos(x2) + cos(x1) sin(x2), with the four factors B32 values from
# tables, evaluated with one FMA in B32 and rounded once to BF16. For |x| >= 4096, |x| has at most 8 significant
# bits b0 2^i + ... + b7 2^(i+7), and the sine and cosine of each power 2^(i+j) come from tables, combined by the
# addition formulas. Round to nearest only.
#
# Also home to the tables cos, tan and sin_cos share: sin and cos of x1 and of x2.
#
# Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binaryb16/sin/sin_bf16.c.
# Copyright (c) 2025 Paul Zimmermann
# MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module System/Numerics/BF16

